# Check out LF on every platform, including Windows.
#
# tests/renderer-wiring.test.js and tests/ui-regressions.test.js assert against
# literal source text with regexes that contain \n. Git for Windows converts LF
# to CRLF on checkout by default, which silently breaks any pattern needing two
# consecutive newlines: \n\n becomes \n\r\n and never matches. That took the
# Windows release validation down and blocked publishing.
#
# text=auto still detects binaries, so images and archives are left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
